[32m+[m[32m## ⚖️ 12. Phase 7: Class Imbalance Handling & Optimization Summary[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAn empirical investigation was conducted across 6 class imbalance handling techniques using strict Stratified 5-Fold Cross-Validation on the training data ($N=2,620$, zero test leakage):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### A. Training Class Distribution[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Class 0 (Not Potable / Unsafe)**: **1,598 samples (60.99%)**[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Class 1 (Potable / Safe)**: **1,022 samples (39.01%)**[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Imbalance Ratio**: **1.564 : 1** (Moderate Imbalance)[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Artifact**: [artifacts/class_distribution.png](file:///c:/Users/balaj/OneDrive/Desktop/project_1/artifacts/class_distribution.png)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### B. Experimental Results at Threshold 0.50 (5-Fold CV Out-of-Fold, $N=2,620$):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Experiment | Technique | Accuracy | Balanced Accuracy | Recall (C1) | Precision (C1) | F1-Score (C1) | Recall (C0) | ROC-AUC |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Exp A** | No Resampling (Baseline) | 0.6683 | 0.6013 | 0.2965 | **0.6689** | 0.4108 | **0.9061** | 0.6849 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Exp B** | Random Oversampling | 0.6672 | 0.6242 | 0.4286 | 0.6033 | 0.5011 | 0.8198 | 0.6862 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Exp C** | **Random Undersampling (Winner)** | 0.6401 | **0.6318** | **0.5939** | 0.5348 | **0.5628** | 0.6696 | 0.6796 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Exp D** | SMOTE Synthetic Oversampling | 0.6542 | 0.6301 | 0.5205 | 0.5612 | 0.5401 | 0.7397 | 0.6850 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Exp E** | Class Weight (`balanced`) | **0.6698** | 0.6117 | 0.3474 | 0.6420 | 0.4508 | 0.8761 | **0.6921** |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Exp F** | Balanced Subsample | 0.6630 | 0.6031 | 0.3307 | 0.6294 | 0.4336 | 0.8755 | 0.6867 |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### C. Key Findings & Trade-Offs[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Best Imbalance Technique**: **Random Undersampling (Exp C)** achieved the highest Balanced Accuracy (**0.6318**) and doubled Class 1 Recall to **59.39%** (capturing 607 potable samples vs. 303 in baseline).[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Overall Accuracy Trade-Off**: Overall accuracy decreased slightly from 66.83% to 64.01% (-2.82 percentage points) due to the inherent trade-off of reducing majority-class false reassurance.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Imbalance Handling vs. Threshold Tuning**: Both Random Undersampling at $\tau = 0.50$ (Balanced Accuracy: 0.6318, Class 1 Recall: 59.39%) and Threshold Tuning at $\tau = 0.40$ on the baseline model (Balanced Accuracy: 0.6336, Class 1 Recall: 57.83%) achieve virtually identical operating points. However, Threshold Tuning preserves all training data without discarding samples.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Model Preservation**: The production champion model (`models/best_model.joblib`) and active threshold configuration (`artifacts/threshold_config.json`, $\tau = 0.40$) remain active and protected. The winning experimental model is archived separately under [models/experiments/best_imbalance_model.joblib](file:///c:/Users/balaj/OneDrive/Desktop/project_1/models/experiments/best_imbalance_model.joblib).[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Comprehensive Technical Report**: For detailed methodology and diagnostic plots, see [artifacts/phase_7_report.md](file:///c:/Users/balaj/OneDrive/Desktop/project_1/artifacts/phase_7_report.md).[m
